1f:["$","$L2e",null,{"type":"multiple","children":[["$","$L2f",null,{"title":"Is Forge open source?","id":"is-forge-open-source","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"It is source-available today and open source on a timer. The FSL 1.1\ngrant permits everything except offering Forge itself as a\ncompeting commercial service, and each release converts to Apache 2.0\ntwo years after publication. If your concern is \"can I read and modify\nthe code that runs my builds\", the answer is yes, without qualification."}]}],["$","$L2f",null,{"title":"Can I use it commercially?","id":"can-i-use-it-commercially","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"Yes. Running it to build your own software is a permitted purpose,\ncommercial or not. The restriction is on reselling Forge as a\ncompeting product or service. The two BUSL modules are the ones to\ncheck with counsel if you plan to redistribute."}]}],["$","$L2f",null,{"title":"Why Rust and not Go?","id":"why-rust-and-not-go","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"Predictable tail latency without a garbage collector, and memory safety\nwithout a managed runtime. The cost is compile time and a smaller pool\nof contributors, a real trade, made deliberately, for a component whose\nworst failure mode is silently serving the wrong bytes."}]}],["$","$L2f",null,{"title":"Does the version number mean anything?","id":"does-the-version-number-mean-anything","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Less than it looks like. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"compatibility_level = 0"}]," in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"MODULE.bazel"}],"\nmeans no cross-version compatibility guarantee. Read the changelog\nbefore upgrading, and pin the version in your deployment."]}]}]]}]
20:["$","a",null,{"href":"/explanations/lre","data-next-step":"next","className":"my-4 flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 no-underline transition-colors border-brand/40 bg-brand-soft/30 hover:border-brand/70","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"18","height":"18","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"mt-1 shrink-0 text-brand","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6"}]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block font-mono text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-muted-foreground","children":"Next"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"block font-semibold text-foreground","children":"Local Remote Execution"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 block text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"The idea that came out of the rewrite rather than driving it: the same\nhermetic toolchain on your laptop and on the remote workers."}]}]]}]]}]
